# Every endpoint, in the order you would try them against `docker compose up`.
# The tokens are the compose file's local-only values.

@api = http://127.0.0.1:5190
@read = walrus-read-token-for-local-use-only
@operator = walrus-operator-token-for-local-use-only

### Liveness and readiness. Ready means the store answers; capture reconnecting during a failover does not
### make the API unready.
GET {{api}}/health/ready

### Without a token: 401.
GET {{api}}/v1/stats

### Sources and sinks in one call: where capture is attached, how much log each slot is holding, whether the
### standby could take over, and each sink's lag.
GET {{api}}/v1/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}

### A replica of two tables in the sink database, bootstrapped from a consistent snapshot and then streamed.
### "target" names a configured connection; the connection string itself never goes through the API.
POST {{api}}/v1/sinks
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "replica",
  "kind": "Postgres",
  "tables": ["public.accounts", "public.profiles"],
  "target": "replica",
  "start": "Snapshot"
}

### An in-memory search index over the same tables, rebuilt from the outbox on every start.
POST {{api}}/v1/sinks
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "search",
  "kind": "Index",
  "tables": ["public.accounts", "public.profiles"],
  "start": "Beginning"
}

### A webhook. Refused unless the host is in Walrus:WebhookAllowedHosts, which compose leaves empty, so this
### shows the refusal.
POST {{api}}/v1/sinks
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "hook",
  "kind": "Webhook",
  "tables": ["public.accounts"],
  "target": "http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data",
  "start": "Now"
}

### The read token can look but not change: 401.
POST {{api}}/v1/sinks
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "nope", "kind": "Index", "tables": ["public.accounts"], "start": "Now" }

### One sink: its position in each source, and its lag.
GET {{api}}/v1/sinks/replica
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}

### Rows in the index containing every word.
GET {{api}}/v1/sinks/search/search?q=linus
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}

### Changes a sink refused, with the reason. Empty unless something was refused.
GET {{api}}/v1/sinks/replica/dead-letters
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}

### Retry them, oldest first per row, once the sink is fixed.
POST {{api}}/v1/sinks/replica/dead-letters/retry
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}

### Redeliver everything from the start of the outbox. Nothing changes: each row's state recognises every change.
POST {{api}}/v1/sinks/replica/replay
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}

### Empty the sink and rebuild it from a log position.
POST {{api}}/v1/sinks/replica/replay?fromLsn=0/0&reset=true
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}

### Rebuild from a fresh consistent snapshot.
POST {{api}}/v1/sinks/replica/snapshot
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}

### The most recent conflict decisions: which change lost, and to which source's newer write.
GET {{api}}/v1/conflicts
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}

### The live feed, as server-sent events. Leave it open and write to a source.
GET {{api}}/v1/events
Authorization: Bearer {{read}}

### Remove a sink, with its cursors and dead letters.
DELETE {{api}}/v1/sinks/search
Authorization: Bearer {{operator}}

### The OpenAPI document the console's types are generated from.
GET {{api}}/openapi/v1.json
